FerrionOS change to Redox base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with ferrion-boot-splash.patch applied (security roadmap S13, lockdown). It needs ferrion-lockdown.patch of the kernel recipe, which adds the memory scheme's restricted root and port-io handle:
- the hardware right is a property of a namespace handle. The namespace manager gives it to the boot process alone; a handle without it does not open, list, fork, register or remove irq, serio, kernel.acpi, pci and acpi, and its memory is the kernel's restricted root. A ShrinkPermissions request keeps the right only with the bit 1 << 63, which libredox does not define. An open of a hidden scheme logs the caller's pid and the scheme;
- init starts a service without the right unless its unit sets `hardware = true`, and every script command without it, through daemon::without_hardware; the units of the drivers and driver managers set it (rtcd, lived, vesad, bcm2835-sdhcid, hwd, both pcid-spawner units, ps2d, and redoxfs, which reads the disk password from the physical address the bootloader passes);
- drivers get I/O ports from /scheme/memory/port-io instead of the thread handle's Iopl verb;
- a driver's memory root and PCI channel are close-on-exec, xhcid starts USB class drivers without the right, and redoxerd starts its command without it.

